# EffortDataTools 

<!-- badges: start -->
[![R-CMD-check](https://github.com/afsc-gap-products/racehauls/actions/workflows/R-CMD-check.yaml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/afsc-gap-products/racehauls/actions)
[![Lifecycle: experimental](https://img.shields.io/badge/lifecycle-experimental-orange.svg)](https://lifecycle.r-lib.org/articles/stages.html#experimental)
<!-- badges: end -->

The **`EffortDataTools`** package provides utility functions for fisheries scientists and data managers working with NOAA Fisheries Resource Assessment and Conservation Engineering (RACE) groundfish survey data. 

It streamlines three common workflows:
1. Extracting filtered **repick haul records** directly from Oracle RACE databases.
2. Merging and time-trimming **Scientific Computing System (SCS) XML** data streams.
3. Visualizing **haul tracks** overlaid on survey grid cell maps shaded by depth strata.

---

## Installation

You can install the development version of `racehauls` directly from GitHub using `pak` or `remotes`:

```r
# install.packages("pak")
pak::pak("afsc-gap-products/racehauls")

# Or via remotes:
# remotes::install_github("afsc-gap-products/racehauls")